<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-1968] Hive JDBC proxy user hardcoded, couldn&apos;t it be passed as an option ?</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1968</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Hi,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hive Connection is done through proxy users like this : &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;if (&quot;hive&quot;.equalsIgnoreCase(propertyKey)) &lt;/p&gt;
{
                connection = getConnectionFromPool(url + &quot;;hive.server2.proxy.user=&quot; + user,
                  user, propertyKey, properties);
              }
&lt;p&gt; else {&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It&apos;s hardcoded, so if someone doesn&apos;t want to use proxy users, he has to made some changes to the code and then rebuild Zeppelin from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Couln&apos;t this be passed as a parameter ?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&lt;p&gt;Ubuntu 14.04&lt;/p&gt;</environment>
